                        "target_lang_word": "habanera",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "habanera",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "c272ed97-33d3-35fa-8558-c6491f85af28",
                                        "entry_id": "7998d9bd-2743-33a1-a374-1fa7d7651cb7",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A style of music from Cuba."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b99822a9-ed43-4313-a7fb-f64ac4397a38",
                                                "sense_id": "c272ed97-33d3-35fa-8558-c6491f85af28",
                                                "text": "The programming was far from random. The habanera is a hybrid seed of great potency. An adaptation of the European contradanza by slaves from West Africa, it is not only an early version of a New World rhythm that took over the globe, but also a direct ancestor for much of jazz and rock ‘n’ roll."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "c5a635e2-1adb-3142-8bee-df39e8403685",
                                        "entry_id": "7998d9bd-2743-33a1-a374-1fa7d7651cb7",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A dance performed to this music."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f3bee4cc-022c-47c7-821b-ea247b0e019b",
                                                "sense_id": "c5a635e2-1adb-3142-8bee-df39e8403685",
                                                "text": "The music of Cuba has had a worldwide influence on forms of song and dance. René Buch who conceived and directed a musical “collage” called “¡Habana!” at the Repertorio Español on East 27th Street, points out the influence on Spain, for example, which received ‘habaneras’ and ‘contradanzas’ from Cuba; in this century, in the 1920's, the “rumba” and such songs as “El Manisero” and “Siboney” made their way north to become part of United States culture."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "21ca4721-2a51-4d1a-b714-077c5386801f",
                        "source_entry_id": "81826491-7767-30f7-9a91-fccaffc31f7c",
                        "source_sense_id": "85222bd0-9cf9-3ee6-ad42-e392e46ef7f9",
                        "source_sense_description": "Tanz: aus Kuba stammender Tanz im ruhigen Zweivierteltakt",
                        "target_lang_word": "habanera",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "habanera",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "ce96d473-e572-32a9-a509-96b4f4e5a6d3",
                                        "entry_id": "1262eacf-8e2e-32d5-a095-8548ef85c2d8",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Danse et musique cubaine nées en 1830 à Cuba."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0b941893-cf24-4f14-b722-3055010f1cb0",
                                                "sense_id": "ce96d473-e572-32a9-a509-96b4f4e5a6d3",
                                                "text": "En fait Nane lui était d’aussi peu de produit qu’un buisson de roses, un hamac, une habanera ; et l’on ignorera toujours pourquoi il conservait une employée aussi coûteuse."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6c8e82a8-cd1e-4c23-b79a-5869e41b77f6",
                                                "sense_id": "ce96d473-e572-32a9-a509-96b4f4e5a6d3",
                                                "text": "Pour le divertissement de quelques touristes, un manager avait organisé une soirée de danses […]. Habanera, cachucha, séguedille authentiques nous furent servies ce soir-là."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4a73eae8-e55c-4b7d-9257-5dfe3f869f8b",
                                                "sense_id": "ce96d473-e572-32a9-a509-96b4f4e5a6d3",
                                                "text": "Les jours de fête\nQuand les indiens et les vaqueros s’enivrent de whisky et de pulque\nDorypha danse\nAu son de la guitare mexicaine\nHabaneras si entraînantes\nQu’on vient de plusieurs lieues pour l’admirer"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
